From 826eb187bf474a07465fb0bc4a5035024ff626b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Alvaro=20Garz=C3=B3n?= <eduardo831_@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:54:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] analysis: accept external hints (code ranges, seeds, jump
 tables)

psp_analyze and psp_recomp --auto only see what their own heuristics find.
Disassemblers such as Ghidra find more (function starts after returns,
pointers formed far from their use, switch tables), so let a profile pass
that knowledge in without putting any title address in the framework:

  code <start> <end>                 replaces the PT_LOAD-derived ranges
  seed <address> [source]            extra function entry
  jumptable <jr address> <target>... targets of an indirect jump

load_analysis_hints() reads that text format, analyze_program() gets an
overload that takes AnalysisHints, and both tools accept --hints <file>.
Jump-table targets become blocks of the function that owns the jr, so they
are emitted and registered as dispatcher entries. Without --hints nothing
changes. PSPRECOMP_ANALYSIS_HINTS lets tools test for the feature.

Code ranges matter for PRX modules: their first PT_LOAD also holds .rodata,
so the automatic ranges decode data as code.
